From: Qiliang Yuan <odys.yuan@gmail.com>
Subject: selftests/mm: move waiting for KSM full scans into a helper
Date: Sat, 07 Nov 2026 11:57:02 -0500

ksm_start() enables ksmd and then polls full_scans until two more full
scans have completed, so that any merging that can happen has happened.

There is no helper to wait for a number of full scans while ksmd is
already running, so a test that needs one has to copy that loop.

Move the loop into ksm_wait_full_scans() and make ksm_start() call it
after enabling ksmd. The count is now read after ksmd starts rather than
before, which can only make ksm_start() wait longer.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/20261107-bug-mm-ksm-smart-scan-align-skips-v3-3-16d5ce8b5fd6@gmail.com
Signed-off-by: Qiliang Yuan <odys.yuan@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Reviewed-by: David Hildenbrand (Arm) <david@kernel.org>
Cc: Xu Xin <xu.xin@linux.dev>
Cc: Chengming Zhou <chengming.zhou@linux.dev>
Cc: Stefan Roesch <shr@devkernel.io>
Cc: Lorenzo Stoakes <ljs@kernel.org>
Cc: Liam R. Howlett <liam@infradead.org>
Cc: Vlastimil Babka <vbabka@kernel.org>
Cc: Mike Rapoport <rppt@kernel.org>
Cc: Suren Baghdasaryan <surenb@google.com>
Cc: Michal Hocko <mhocko@suse.com>
Cc: Shuah Khan <shuah@kernel.org>
Cc: Jonathan Corbet <corbet@lwn.net>
Cc: Shuah Khan <skhan@linuxfoundation.org>
Cc: Randy Dunlap <rdunlap@infradead.org>
---

 tools/testing/selftests/mm/vm_util.c |   31 ++++++++++++++-----------
 tools/testing/selftests/mm/vm_util.h |    1 
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

--- a/tools/testing/selftests/mm/vm_util.c~selftests-mm-move-waiting-for-ksm-full-scans-into-a-helper
+++ a/tools/testing/selftests/mm/vm_util.c
@@ -984,33 +984,38 @@ int ksm_use_zero_pages(void)
 	return ret == 1 ? 0 : -errno;
 }
 
+int ksm_wait_full_scans(long nr)
+{
+	long start_scans, end_scans;
+
+	start_scans = ksm_get_full_scans();
+	if (start_scans < 0)
+		return start_scans;
+	do {
+		end_scans = ksm_get_full_scans();
+		if (end_scans < 0)
+			return end_scans;
+	} while (end_scans < start_scans + nr);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 int ksm_start(void)
 {
 	int ksm_fd;
 	ssize_t ret;
-	long start_scans, end_scans;
 
 	ksm_fd = open("/sys/kernel/mm/ksm/run", O_RDWR);
 	if (ksm_fd < 0)
 		return -errno;
 
-	/* Wait for two full scans such that any possible merging happened. */
-	start_scans = ksm_get_full_scans();
-	if (start_scans < 0) {
-		close(ksm_fd);
-		return start_scans;
-	}
 	ret = write(ksm_fd, "1", 1);
 	close(ksm_fd);
 	if (ret != 1)
 		return -errno;
-	do {
-		end_scans = ksm_get_full_scans();
-		if (end_scans < 0)
-			return end_scans;
-	} while (end_scans < start_scans + 2);
 
-	return 0;
+	/* Wait for two full scans such that any possible merging happened. */
+	return ksm_wait_full_scans(2);
 }
 
 int ksm_stop(void)
--- a/tools/testing/selftests/mm/vm_util.h~selftests-mm-move-waiting-for-ksm-full-scans-into-a-helper
+++ a/tools/testing/selftests/mm/vm_util.h
@@ -162,6 +162,7 @@ void *sys_mremap(void *old_address, unsi
 long ksm_get_self_zero_pages(void);
 long ksm_get_self_merging_pages(void);
 long ksm_get_full_scans(void);
+int ksm_wait_full_scans(long nr);
 int ksm_use_zero_pages(void);
 int ksm_start(void);
 int ksm_stop(void);
_
